# width: 120
# height: 40
# The focus cue in a light theme (`ui/focus_cue.zig`): the dim role and
# the rail's step-back are derived from the theme's contrast — never
# under 2.0:1 on the ground, the pane's hue kept. catppuccin-latte's
# palette dim (#8b97b9) sat 1.09:1 from its focused name (#7287fd) and
# its stepped-back green rail (#add2a8) 1.48:1 on the ground. Every
# theme's floors are the unit test "every bundled theme keeps the focus
# cue and the needs-you mark visible" (`ui/theme.zig`).
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex colorscheme catppuccin-latte
expect screen contains "alpha"
command view.focus_pane
# The focused name steps up from the pale lavender to 3:1.
expect color 34 1 fg #6372c5
expect color 31 5 fg #40a02b
command view.focus_tree
expect color 34 1 fg not #8b97b9
expect color 34 1 fg #8994cf
expect color 31 5 fg not #add2a8
expect color 31 5 fg #7cbb70
ex colorscheme one_light
command view.focus_tree
expect color 31 5 fg not #bad8b9
expect color 31 5 fg #8cc08c
expect color 34 1 fg not #a2a2a3
expect color 34 1 fg #9a9a9e
